Vectorwake is a Subspace-like MMO. Constitution vendored; American spelling; drill A/B for balance. Admin is an operator console with no-IP activity logs. Tiers: Newb/Wing/Lead/Ace/Legend. Controls single-source; H/? table remains, no trigger help. Site mark 18x22/9px.                  
Built the public site and the shared logo, planned the launch, then spent a long stretch hardening the client before moving the fleet to Dallas.                                                                                                                                               
Hardened the network lifecycle and lag telemetry, moved the fleet to Dallas, fixed and measured the bot skill dial, shipped trails and wall light, then Chris's rethink became the match game: 3-min 4v4 melee, kits replace greens, bounty = base + run, gunners and Alpha cut.               
The match game got its whole front end, built to the mocks and then played into shape: shop, friends, bots, ship page, standings, map editor and the CI gates around them.                                                                                                                     
Aug 2026: audits fixed determinism, round identity, prediction and the settings wire; the ladder and bounty settled on rivets and signed evidence; then a long pass over the client's screens for the match game, and mines were taken out of the game entirely.                               
